{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'precondition|path|snapshot|replac|private|trusted' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,80p'; head -32 poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json; cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/b5kzzw3xn.output; python3 -B -c 'import sys;print(sys.executable,sys.version)'; ls -d .venv*; rg -n '28 of 29|28/29|36 passed|36 pass|pipe opened blocking' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"12:- **A store path whose resolved form holds `%`, `?` or `#` is refused** (`release.store_path`), because `store.open_read_only` puts\n13:  the path into a SQLite `file:` URI unescaped (test 24). The opener itself is shared POC code and is not changed here.\n17:  - `store_path` returns the resolved path, which the opener is given, so a link is not resolved twice (test 24);\n48:- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\n54:74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\n59:- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\n70:build or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\n72:- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\n76:symbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\n97:- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\n133:  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\n156:- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\n176:  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\n184:- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\n185:  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\n189:  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\n191:  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\n194:  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\n195:- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\n207:  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\n214:  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\n216:  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\n229:  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\n232:  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\n239:  - the store path and the bound;\n262:| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n263:| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n266:| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n271:| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\n275:| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n279:| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n280:| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n299:| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n312:## 4. New path × old checks\n314:| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\n319:| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\n320:| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\n340:The fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\n357:8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\n395:18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\n431:- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\n433:- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\n435:- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\n439:- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\n{\n \"stores\": {\n  \"old-1\": {\n   \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\",\n   \"counts\": {\n    \"questions\": {\n     \"number\": 19,\n     \"event\": 28,\n     \"yes_no\": 0\n    },\n    \"evidence\": 8251,\n    \"sources\": 8251,\n    \"fields_compared\": 91055\n   },\n   \"withheld_unresolved\": 0,\n   \"unresolved\": [],\n   \"data_bytes\": 5788634,\n   \"library_bytes\": 14478536,\n   \"seconds\": 8.55,\n   \"library_seconds\": 6.69,\n   \"bytes_within_budget\": true,\n   \"seconds_within_budget\": true,\n   \"diagnostics\": {\n    \"stored_strings_judged\": 6670,\n    \"package_strings\": 91012,\n    \"judgement_columns_absent\": [],\n    \"hits\": [\n     {\n      \"stored_in\": \"v11\",\n      \"kind\": \"switch reason\",\n      \"text\": \"created\",\n      \"found_in\": \"v3\",\nok\n# Council round 75c: re-review the built slice 1 after round 75's fixes (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n\nRounds 75 and 75b (`codex-r75.md`, `codex-r75b.md`) did not accept slice 1. Claude fixed the code, the tests, the mutant\nrunner and the check script, and recorded the changes:\n- `RELEASE-BUILD.md`, its revision 11 block;\n- `RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`, rewritten from the new run `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json`.\n\nThe files are `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`, and in that folder `release_mutants.py`\nand `release_check.py`.\n\n/Users/lchingen/.pyenv/versions/3.10.10/bin/python3 3.10.10 (main, Apr 17 2025, 14:51:11) [Clang 16.0.0 (clang-1600.0.26.3)]\nzsh:1: no matches found: .venv*\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:28:    'pipe opened blocking': (R, \"os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\", \"os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, dir_fd=folder)\"),\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75c.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md; rg -n 'revision 11|Revision 11|\\\"'^#'\\\"' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release, slice 1: built and checked at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Result.** Slice 1 is built to `RELEASE-BUILD.md`:\\n     4\\t- revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten review rounds;\\n     5\\t- revision 11 records what councils 75 and 75b required of the build.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\tIt passes its tests, its mutants and the $0 release check on four stored stores. Nothing is committed, published or deployed. The POC\\n     8\\tis unchanged; no POC code imports the release module.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\\n    11\\t- Check: `release_check.py`; mutants: `release_mutants.py` (both in this folder).\\n    12\\t- Output: `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/`. The runs `release-check-2026-11-23/` and `-23b/` predate the fixes of councils 75\\n    13\\t  and 75b and are kept for the record; their numbers are the same.\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\t## 1. Council 75's findings, and what changed\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\tCouncil 75 (`codex-r75.md`) reproduced the four packages' counts and both refusals of the substituted forecast. It did not accept the\\n    18\\tslice. Its findings and the fixes:\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\\n    21\\t|---|---|---|\\n    22\\t| A key written after the bound could reclassify an earlier package (the key lookup ignored its `seq`) | the key counts only when visible at the bound | test 22; mutant \\\"key read without its day\\\" |\\n    23\\t| Ten text fields accepted null, which revision 10 forbids | strings only | test 23; mutant \\\"null accepted as text\\\" |\\n    24\\t| `check` read the data file three times: it could hash one version and certify another | one read through one folder handle; hash and parse the same bytes; the command reports that data | structural (`check_package`) |\\n    25\\t| A path holding `%` could make SQLite open a different file from the one named | `release.store_path` refuses `%`, `?`, `#` | test 24; mutant \\\"store-path refusal removed\\\" |\\n    26\\t| Test 14's marker case supplied the very line its mutant removes | the instrumentation no longer touches the line that drops the staging path | test 14; mutant caught |\\n    27\\t| Test 13 damaged two things | the package copy keeps `e2` with no source, which is what a checker that drops missing items expects | test 13; mutant \\\"inner join\\\" caught |\\n    28\\t| Tests 1, 2 and 9 lacked decisive assertions | test 25 proves the writer's own refusal; test 2 checks all five labels in `v1`'s own fields; test 9 names each refusal's reason | mutants caught |\\n    29\\t| The mutant runner counted any non-zero exit | it stops on a failing control, and counts a catch only with a failing test and no setup or collection error | run below |\\n    30\\t| My first result overstated the closing check, the diagnostic search and the dated check, and the script never failed | corrected below; the script now fails on any missed acceptance item or budget | this run |\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\t**Council 75b** (`codex-r75b.md`) confirmed the fixes above and found four more gaps, now fixed:\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\\n    35\\t|---|---|---|\\n    36\\t| The store-path check returned the original path, which the opener resolved again | `store_path` returns the resolved path, and the opener is given that | test 24 (a symbolic link); mutant \\\"store path returned unresolved\\\" |\\n    37\\t| A named pipe in a package would make `check` hang instead of refusing | files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), then refused by type | test 15, through the command with a 30 s bound; mutant \\\"pipe opened blocking\\\" |\\n    38\\t| The check script could pass with a required example missing | the three examples are a fixed list; a missing one fails the script | this run |\\n    39\\t| No test reordered records, and the runner credited a failure of a test's own scratch edit | test 10 reorders questions and evidence; scratch edits fail with \\\"scratch anchor\\\", which the runner does not count | mutant \\\"check_origins accepting another order\\\" |\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\tIt also asked that test 23 cover all ten text fields (now one case per field) and that test 2 check every question's own fields for\\n    42\\tthe labels (done).\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t**No regression.**\\n    45\\t- The release tests: 36 pass. The full suite passed with 416 tests before council 75b's changes; it is re-run in the next step.\\n    46\\t- Mutants: 28 of 29 are caught by failing tests, not counting scratch-edit failures, with no setup errors.\\n    47\\t- **The 29th, the canonical-day check removed, is equivalent on this repository's Python 3.10.10,** whose `date.fromisoformat` already\\n    48\\t  refuses `20260825`. Under Python 3.13, on a temporary copy of `old-1` with one later completed day:\\n    49\\t  - the real code refuses `20260825`;\\n    50\\t  - the mutant exports `v8` with 1,284 pieces of evidence through 2026-09-20 into a package dated 2026-08-25, where the right package\\n    51\\t    holds 621.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t## 2. The $0 release check (design §7)\\n    54\\t\\n    55\\t| Store | Bound | Number / event / Yes-No | Evidence | Fields compared | Data bytes (library) | Seconds (library) |\\n    56\\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n    57\\t| old-1 | 2026-09-20 | 19 / 28 / 0 | 8,251 | 91,055 | 5,788,634 (14,478,536) | 8.59 (6.77) |\\n    58\\t| old-2 | 2026-09-20 | 17 / 26 / 0 | 6,306 | 69,636 | 4,427,609 (11,893,701) | 6.47 (5.11) |\\n    59\\t| old-3 | 2026-09-20 | 18 / 31 / 0 | 6,659 | 73,559 | 4,685,247 (12,375,915) | 6.78 (5.45) |\\n    60\\t| served | 2026-08-28 | 13 / 55 / 0 | 6,461 | 71,524 | 4,612,321 (12,145,774) | 4.49 (3.50) |\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\t- **Every package passed its origin check:** every field compared with its stored source at the bound.\\n    63\\t- **No number question is unresolved** in these stores.\\n    64\\t- **Budgets met:**\\n    65\\t  - the bytes are 0.37–0.40 of the existing library's;\\n    66\\t  - the seconds are 1.24–1.28 times the library's, against a budget of 3 times and 120 s.\\n    67\\t- **How the evidence is counted.** The count includes each piece once per question that holds it. Every piece has exactly one source\\n    68\\t  row (`old-1`: 5,390 rows for 5,390 pieces).\\n    69\\t- **The script exits non-zero on any missed acceptance item** (each example, refusal, leak, control and closing check named in it) or\\n    70\\t  budget; this run ended \\\"every acceptance item and budget met\\\".\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t**The decisive acceptance case** (council 74, `old-1`):\\n    73\\t- **Kept, equal to the store:**\\n    74\\t  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\\n    75\\t  - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`, under `v4`, `v5`, `v8`);\\n    76\\t  - the analysts' \\\"$390 billion\\\" (`e3597`, under `v4`, `v5`).\\n    77\\t- **The system's own forecast** (`j1580` implied outcome, \\\"About $390 billion: …\\\"):\\n    78\\t  - substituted into `e2295`'s summary, it is refused, naming `question v8.evidence e2295.one_line`;\\n    79\\t  - added to the manifest, it is refused, naming the off-list key.\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t**The other checks:**\\n    82\\t- **`old-1/v8`:** class `number`, marked \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\". Its 1,284 pieces of evidence are the same ids as `service.evidence` at\\n    83\\t  the bound.\\n    84\\t- **The known Yes/No leaks at their own days.**\\n    85\\t  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there.\\n    86\\t  - Both keep \\\"Yes\\\".\\n    87\\t  - The full explanation and reason texts are absent.\\n    88\\t  - So are the judgements' own phrases: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\", \\\"rung 4\\\", \\\"at rung\\\" and \\\"capex at rung\\\" occur in no field.\\n    89\\t- **Control:** event `old-1/v3` keeps \\\"Yes\\\" and its evidence, equal to the store.\\n    90\\t- **Closing,** on a copy of `old-1` with a closing switch for `v8`, \\\"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\\\":\\n    91\\t  - `bundle.view_bundle` exposes it;\\n    92\\t  - the package shows `open: false`;\\n    93\\t  - the reason appears nowhere.\\n    94\\t  - The word \\\"Bullish\\\" does occur inside six `v8` fields: five source titles and the genuine `e1865` quote. That is source wording,\\n    95\\t    which the design keeps.\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t## 3. The diagnostic search, every hit read\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\tThe search covered every decoded string of each package, ids, classes, the marker and the manifest included. For each question it\\n   100\\ttook every stored string the package must not hold:\\n   101\\t- rung labels of number questions;\\n   102\\t- the rung conditions of every question;\\n   103\\t- judgement reasons, explanations, implied outcomes and references, where the store has those columns (the served ledger lacks the\\n   104\\t  last two);\\n   105\\t- every switch reason, \\\"created\\\" included.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t| Store | Stored strings judged | Package strings | Hits |\\n   108\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   109\\t| old-1 | 6,670 | 91,012 | 1,378: \\\"created\\\" 987, \\\"Bullish\\\" 391 |\\n   110\\t| old-2 | 6,677 | 69,597 | 771: \\\"created\\\" 516, \\\"Bullish\\\" 255 |\\n   111\\t| old-3 | 7,045 | 73,514 | 1,613: \\\"created\\\" 1,176, labels 437 (\\\"Bullish\\\", \\\"High\\\", \\\"Low\\\", \\\"Bearish\\\", \\\"Middle\\\") |\\n   112\\t| served | 2,149 | 71,460 | 1,794: \\\"created\\\" 1,632, \\\"Bullish\\\" 162 |\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\t- **No condition, reason, explanation, implied outcome, reference or closing reason is found anywhere.**\\n   115\\t- **The label hits are 257 package fields holding 32 distinct texts, all read.** Every one is source wording:\\n   116\\t  - headlines: \\\"Jensen Huang's Bullish Call …\\\", \\\"Stock Traded Lower\\\", \\\"Earnings Call Highlights\\\", \\\"Lows Not Seen Since 2019\\\",\\n   117\\t    \\\"Sky-High P/E\\\", \\\"That Bearish Bet\\\";\\n   118\\t  - the memory term \\\"High Bandwidth Memory\\\";\\n   119\\t  - the analyst quote \\\"Bullish confirmation would require …\\\".\\n   120\\t- **The \\\"created\\\" hits fall in 33 distinct texts, all containing the ordinary word.** It is every question's creation reason and\\n   121\\t  carries no forecast.\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t## 4. Not shown, and still open\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t- **The reader's screen** (slice 2, D756's screen check) is not built. The release page must read only this package, with no live\\n   126\\t  fetch and no idea submission, and needs a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen.\\n   127\\t- **The idea path in the release:** deferred (council 74); its acceptance is pending.\\n   128\\t- **The recorded disagreement on evidence summaries** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8) stands.\\n   129\\t- **`store.open_read_only` puts a path into a SQLite URI unescaped.** That is shared POC code; the release refuses such paths\\n   130\\t  rather than changing it.\\n1:# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n3:**Status: revision 11. Built** (`src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`; result in\\n4:`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`). Revision 10 was ready per council 74j; revision 11 records the changes council 75 required of the build.\\n6:**Revision 11 (council 75, `codex-r75.md`).** Each change is in the code and has a test and a mutant:\\n87:## 0. Scope\\n107:## 1. What is built\\n246:## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n283:## 3. Value × reader\\n312:## 4. New path × old checks\\n326:## 5. Prior decisions\\n338:## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n441:## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n477:## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75c.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,32p;89,245p;338,476p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"RELEASE-BUILD.md §6 mutants: each applied to a scratch copy (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE, no __pycache__) must fail\\n     2\\ttests/test_release.py; the unmutated control must pass.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     3\\timport shutil\\n     4\\timport subprocess\\n     5\\timport sys\\n     6\\timport tempfile\\n     7\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tREPO = Path('/Users/lchingen/hivemind')\\n    10\\tR, B = 'src/hivemind/release.py', 'scripts/release_build.py'\\n    11\\tMUTANTS = {\\n    12\\t    'condition emitted on number records': (R, \\\"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\\\n            else:\\\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\\\",\\n    13\\t                                            \\\"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\\\n                record['condition'] = 'FY2027 revenue is at least $350 billion'\\\\n            else:\\\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\\\"),\\n    14\\t    'one_line from the latest why_changed': (R, \\\"evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\\\",\\n    15\\t                                             \\\"evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources, 'one_line': (views_db.execute('select why_changed from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone() or {'why_changed': piece['one_line']})['why_changed']})\\\"),\\n    16\\t    'event test removed': (R, \\\"    if key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of) in identity.EVENT_MEASURES:\\\\n        return 'event'\\\\n\\\", ''),\\n    17\\t    'Yes/No test removed': (R, \\\"    if len(labels) == 2 and {vocabulary.canonical('label', label) for label in labels} == {'Yes', 'No'}:\\\\n        return 'yes_no'\\\\n\\\", ''),\\n    18\\t    'check_package without the file-set check': (R, \\\"        if sorted(names) != sorted(PACKAGE_FILES):\\\\n            raise\\\", \\\"        if False:\\\\n            raise\\\"),\\n    19\\t    'manifest keys unchecked': (R, \\\"    _keys(manifest, 'manifest', 'the manifest')\\\\n\\\", ''),\\n    20\\t    'check_export without the closed-key check': (R, \\\"    if set(value) != ALLOWED[kind]:\\\", \\\"    if not set(value) >= ALLOWED[kind]:\\\"),\\n    21\\t    'check_origins skipping evidence fields': (R, \\\"            expected_evidence = _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of)\\\\n\\\",\\n    22\\t                                               \\\"            expected_evidence = question['evidence']\\\\n\\\"),\\n    23\\t    'check_origins taking the class from the package': (R, \\\"            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, as_of)\\\\n            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': _open_at(\\\",\\n    24\\t                                                        \\\"            kind = question['class']\\\\n            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': _open_at(\\\"),\\n    25\\t    'check_origins accepting duplicates': (R, \\\"        packaged = data['questions']\\\\n\\\", \\\"        packaged = list({q['id']: q for q in data['questions']}.values())\\\\n\\\"),\\n    26\\t    'check_origins accepting another order': (R, \\\"        packaged = data['questions']\\\\n\\\",\\n    27\\t                                              \\\"        packaged = sorted(data['questions'], key=lambda q: [r['view_id'] for r in views].index(q['id']) if q['id'] in [r['view_id'] for r in views] else -1)\\\\n\\\"),\\n    28\\t    'pipe opened blocking': (R, \\\"os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\\\", \\\"os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, dir_fd=folder)\\\"),\\n    29\\t    'store path returned unresolved': (R, \\\"        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path may not contain {found}, which the SQLite opener reads as URI syntax')\\\\n    return real\\\",\\n    30\\t                                       \\\"        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path may not contain {found}, which the SQLite opener reads as URI syntax')\\\\n    return path\\\"),\\n    31\\t    'check_origins with an inner join': (R, \\\"            if item is None:\\\\n                raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {row[\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\"]}\\\", \\\"            if item is None:\\\\n                continue\\\\n                raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {row[\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\"]}\\\"),\\n    32\\t    'check without validating the day': (R, \\\"        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else resolve(views_db, data['as_of'])\\\",\\n    33\\t                                         \\\"        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else data['as_of']\\\"),\\n    34\\t    'builder skipping the staged check': (B, \\\"counts, data, size = release.check_package(staged, views_db, items_db, expected_as_of=bound)\\\", \\\"counts, size = release.check_export(data), 0\\\"),\\n    35\\t    'symbolic-link check removed': (R, \\\"os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\\\", \\\"os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\\\"),\\n    36\\t    'duplicate-key check removed': (R, \\\"    if len(names) != len(set(names)):\\\", \\\"    if False:\\\"),\\n    37\\t    'switch reason emitted': (R, \\\"            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': service.is_open_as_of(views_db, view_id, bound), 'class': kind}\\\",\\n    38\\t                              \\\"            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': service.is_open_as_of(views_db, view_id, bound), 'class': kind, 'reason': (views_db.execute('select reason from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)).fetchone() or {'reason': ''})['reason']}\\\"),\\n    39\\t    'missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback': (R, \\\"        if row is None:\\\\n            raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {evidence_id}: source item {input_id} is not in the items database')\\\",\\n    40\\t                                                         \\\"        if row is None:\\\\n            row = {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'source_uri': ''}\\\"),\\n    41\\t    'publish replaced by os.rename': (R, \\\"    rename = _no_replace_rename()\\\\n    if rename is None:\\\", \\\"    rename = lambda source, target: os.rename(source, target) or 0\\\\n    if rename is None:\\\"),\\n    42\\t    'the finally removed': (B, \\\"        if staged is not None:\\\\n            shutil.rmtree(staged)\\\\n\\\", ''),\\n    43\\t    'staging path not dropped after publish': (B, \\\"        staged = None                       # published\\\", \\\"        pass                                # published\\\"),\\n    44\\t    'canonical-day check removed': (R, \\\"    if day.isoformat() != text:\\\\n        raise ReleaseRefused\\\", \\\"    if False:\\\\n        raise ReleaseRefused\\\"),\\n    45\\t    'key read without its day': (R, \\\"    return row['measure'] if row is not None and service.visible(conn, row['seq'], as_of) else None\\\",\\n    46\\t                                 \\\"    return row['measure'] if row is not None else None\\\"),\\n    47\\t    'null accepted as text': (R, \\\"        if not isinstance(value[name], str):\\\", \\\"        if not (isinstance(value[name], str) or value[name] is None):\\\"),\\n    48\\t    'store-path refusal removed': (R, \\\"    if found:\\\\n        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path\\\", \\\"    if False:\\\\n        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path\\\"),\\n    49\\t    'writer self-check removed': (R, \\\"    check_export(data)\\\\n    return data\\\\n\\\", \\\"    return data\\\\n\\\"),\\n    50\\t    'publish_report replaced by os.replace': (R, \\\"        os.link(temporary, path)\\\\n\\\", \\\"        os.replace(temporary, path)\\\\n        open(temporary, 'w').close()\\\\n\\\"),\\n    51\\t}\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\tdef tree(where):\\n    55\\t    root = Path(where)\\n    56\\t    shutil.copytree(REPO / 'src', root / 'src', ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('__pycache__'))\\n    57\\t    shutil.copytree(REPO / 'scripts', root / 'scripts', ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('__pycache__'))\\n    58\\t    (root / 'tests').mkdir()\\n    59\\t    for name in ('test_release.py', 'conftest.py'):\\n    60\\t        shutil.copy(REPO / 'tests' / name, root / 'tests' / name)\\n    61\\t    return root\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\tdef run(root):\\n    65\\t    return subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pytest', 'tests/test_release.py', '-q', '-rf', '-p', 'no:cacheprovider'], cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True,\\n    66\\t                          env={'PATH': '/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin', 'PYTHONPATH': f'{root}/src:{root}/poc', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE': '1', 'HOME': str(Path.home())}, timeout=900)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\twith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as base:\\n    70\\t    control = run(tree(Path(base) / 'control'))\\n    71\\t    print('control:', 'PASS' if control.returncode == 0 else 'FAIL', control.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])\\n    72\\t    if control.returncode != 0:\\n    73\\t        raise SystemExit('the unmutated control fails: no mutant is judged')\\n    74\\t    caught = 0\\n    75\\t    for n, (name, (relative, old, new)) in enumerate(MUTANTS.items()):\\n    76\\t        root = tree(Path(base) / f'm{n}')\\n    77\\t        path = root / relative\\n    78\\t        text = path.read_text()\\n    79\\t        assert text.count(old) == 1, (name, text.count(old))\\n    80\\t        path.write_text(text.replace(old, new))\\n    81\\t        result = run(root)\\n    82\\t        failed = [line.split(' ')[1].split('::')[-1] for line in result.stdout.splitlines()\\n    83\\t                  if line.startswith('FAILED') and 'scratch anchor' not in line]      # a test that failed only on its own scratch edit is not a catch\\n    84\\t        errors = [line for line in result.stdout.splitlines() if line.startswith('ERROR')]\\n    85\\t        verdict = 'CAUGHT' if failed and not errors else 'MISSED' if not errors else 'ERROR'   # a setup or collection error is not a catch\\n    86\\t        caught += verdict == 'CAUGHT'\\n    87\\t        print(f'{verdict}  {name}: {len(failed)} failing: {\\\", \\\".join(failed[:6])}' + (f' | errors: {errors[:2]}' if errors else ''))\\n    88\\t    print(f'{caught} of {len(MUTANTS)} mutants caught')\\n     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 11. Built** (`src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`; result in\\n     4\\t`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`). Revision 10 was ready per council 74j; revision 11 records the changes council 75 required of the build.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 11 (council 75, `codex-r75.md`).** Each change is in the code and has a test and a mutant:\\n     7\\t- **A view key counts only once it is visible at the bound** (its `seq`). A key written later never reclassifies an earlier package\\n     8\\t  (test 22).\\n     9\\t- **Text fields are strings, never null,** as §1 already specified (test 23). The four stores hold no null evidence or item fields.\\n    10\\t- **`check_package` reads each file once,** through one handle on the folder (`O_DIRECTORY | O_NOFOLLOW`, then `O_NOFOLLOW` per file and\\n    11\\t  `fstat`). It hashes and parses the same bytes and returns `(counts, data, bytes)`, so the command reports what was checked.\\n    12\\t- **A store path whose resolved form holds `%`, `?` or `#` is refused** (`release.store_path`), because `store.open_read_only` puts\\n    13\\t  the path into a SQLite `file:` URI unescaped (test 24). The opener itself is shared POC code and is not changed here.\\n    14\\t- **The writer's own refusal** is proved by a scratch-copy pair (test 25).\\n    15\\t- **Both commands print the whole report** before publishing it. Durations use `time.monotonic`. Refusals name the evidence id.\\n    16\\t- **Council 75b** (`codex-r75b.md`):\\n    17\\t  - `store_path` returns the resolved path, which the opener is given, so a link is not resolved twice (test 24);\\n    18\\t  - package files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), so a named pipe is refused by type instead of blocking `check` (test 15);\\n    19\\t  - reordered questions and evidence are tested (test 10). Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n    20\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n    23\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n    24\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n    25\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    26\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    27\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    28\\t- narrow reads;\\n    29\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    30\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    31\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    32\\t- no idea submission.\\n    89\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    90\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    91\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    92\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    93\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    94\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    95\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    96\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    97\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    98\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    99\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n   100\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n   101\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n   102\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n   103\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n   104\\t  - any model call;\\n   105\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 1. What is built\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\t- **Constants:**\\n   112\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n   113\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n   114\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n   115\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n   116\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n   119\\t  |---|---|\\n   120\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n   121\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n   122\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n   123\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n   124\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n   125\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n   128\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n   129\\t    only when the table exists;\\n   130\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n   131\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n   132\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n   133\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n   134\\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\\n   135\\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\\n   136\\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\\n   137\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n   138\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n   139\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n   140\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n   141\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n   142\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n   143\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n   144\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n   145\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   146\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   147\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   148\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   149\\t  - Value checks:\\n   150\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\\n   151\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   152\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   153\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   154\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   155\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   156\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   157\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   158\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   159\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   160\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   161\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   162\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   163\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   164\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   165\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   166\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   167\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   168\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   171\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   172\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   173\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   174\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   175\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   176\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   177\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   178\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   179\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   180\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   181\\t\\n   182\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   183\\t  compared.\\n   184\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   185\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   186\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   187\\t  else.\\n   188\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   189\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   190\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   191\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   192\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   193\\t\\n   194\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   195\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   196\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   197\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   198\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   199\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   200\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   201\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   202\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   203\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   204\\t\\n   205\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   206\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   207\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   208\\t     guarantee;\\n   209\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   210\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   211\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   212\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   213\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   214\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   215\\t     nothing;\\n   216\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\\n   217\\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\\n   218\\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\\n   219\\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   222\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   223\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   224\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   225\\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\\n   226\\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run\\n   227\\t    `check` to write it\\\".\\n   228\\t\\n   229\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   230\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   231\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   232\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\\n   233\\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\\n   234\\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report is not published: its name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else, which stays\\n   235\\t    untouched), or writing the temporary file or the link fails for any other reason, which is printed;\\n   236\\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   237\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   238\\t- **The report:**\\n   239\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   240\\t  - counts per class;\\n   241\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   242\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   243\\t  - bytes;\\n   244\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   245\\t\\n   338\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   339\\t\\n   340\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   341\\tits row above:\\n   342\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   343\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   344\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   345\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   346\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   347\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   348\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   349\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   350\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   351\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   352\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   353\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   354\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   355\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   356\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   357\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   358\\t9. **Package:**\\n   359\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   360\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   361\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   362\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   363\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   364\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   365\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   366\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   367\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   368\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   369\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   370\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   371\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\\n   372\\t    - the build exits 0, and the package and its report exist;\\n   373\\t    - `check` with the build's report still in place prints a passing result and exits 2;\\n   374\\t    - after the test removes that report, `check` exits 0 and publishes a fresh one.\\n   375\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   376\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   377\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   378\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   379\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   380\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   381\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   382\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   383\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   384\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   385\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   386\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   387\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   388\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   389\\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   390\\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\\n   391\\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\\n   392\\t      and inode).\\n   393\\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\\n   394\\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\\n   395\\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\\n   396\\t    case-variant name on this case-insensitive volume, and a symbolic link to it. `build` refuses, and `check` on an existing package\\n   397\\t    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\\n   398\\t19. **Report name taken during the build** (a scratch copy with a pause just before `publish_report`): the test writes a marker file\\n   399\\t    at the report name. The command exits 2 and the marker is unchanged. `check` then prints a passing result, exits 2, and leaves the\\n   400\\t    marker unchanged.\\n   401\\t21. **`check` cannot write its report** (a scratch copy in which creating the report's temporary file raises `PermissionError`): `check`\\n   402\\t    prints the passing result and the write error, and exits 2.\\n   403\\t20. **Temporary file left after the link** (a scratch copy in which removing the report's temporary file raises): the build exits 0\\n   404\\t    and says the report is published, naming the leftover temporary file. The report exists and equals the build's report.\\n   405\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   406\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   407\\t15. **Files:**\\n   408\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   409\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   410\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   411\\t16. **Bound validation:**\\n   412\\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\\n   413\\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\\n   414\\t      the earlier evidence;\\n   415\\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   416\\t\\n   417\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   418\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   419\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   420\\t- the event test removed;\\n   421\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   422\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   423\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   424\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   425\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   426\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   427\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   428\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   429\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   430\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   431\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   432\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   433\\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\\n   434\\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\\n   435\\t- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\\n   436\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   437\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   438\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   439\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   440\\t\\n   441\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   442\\t\\n   443\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   444\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   445\\t\\n   446\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   447\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   448\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   449\\t\\n   450\\tThe steps:\\n   451\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   452\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   453\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   454\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   455\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   456\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   457\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   458\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   459\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   460\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   461\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   462\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   463\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   464\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   465\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   466\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   467\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   468\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   469\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   470\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   471\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   472\\t\\n   473\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   474\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   475\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   476\\t\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:37:| A named pipe in a package would make `check` hang instead of refusing | files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), then refused by type | test 15, through the command with a 30 s bound; mutant \"pipe opened blocking\" |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:45:- The release tests: 36 pass. The full suite passed with 416 tests before council 75b's changes; it is re-run in the next step.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:46:- Mutants: 28 of 29 are caught by failing tests, not counting scratch-edit failures, with no setup errors.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
