{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: slice 1 is not accepted.** I rechecked all four saved packages against their stores and found no off-list field or mismatched value. The production checker also refused both copies containing the substituted `$390 billion` forecast. Three verification gaps remain. [Saved refusals and unchanged control, results.json:44594](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:44594)\n\n1. **The mutant runner can still credit a failed test setup as a catch.** It looks for `scratch anchor` only in pytest’s short `FAILED` line. I reproduced an anchor-only failure under test 12’s name. The traceback contained `scratch anchor`, but the short line contained only the test name. The runner counted that line as a catch. This leaves the report’s claim that 28 catches exclude scratch-edit failures unverified. [release_mutants.py:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:82) · [test_release.py:488](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:488) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:46)\n\n2. **Two tests still pass when the protection they name is removed.** I changed `v6`’s evidence summary to `Bullish` in memory. Test 2 passed because its cross-question label check skips every evidence field. The production checker correctly refused `question v6.evidence e5.one_line`. Test 21 likewise checks only for `passes` and the write error. Removing the line that prints the full report leaves both assertions satisfied. [test_release.py:198](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:198) · [test_release.py:609](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:609) · [release_build.py:31](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:31)\n\n3. **The acceptance script can lose the decisive quote and still pass.** A missing example ID now fails. An ID whose text no longer contains the required example still passes if the package matches the store. In memory, I replaced `e3597`’s analyst `$390 billion` text with `e2295`’s `$361 billion` text on both sides. The script marked `e3597` present and equal, and its final decision returned zero failures. The genuine quote was present in the saved run. [Required control, RELEASE-BUILD.md:456](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:456) · [release_check.py:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:163) · [release_check.py:238](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:238)\n\nThe other round-75 and 75b findings are closed for the reviewed snapshots. The fixes cover historical classification, all ten required text fields, resolved store paths, nonblocking pipe refusal, hashing and parsing the same bytes, and ordered comparisons. The revised staging-marker, missing-item, writer-self-check and hash tests distinguish their intended failures. [release.py:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:87) · [release.py:410](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:410) · [release.py:417](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:417) · [release.py:458](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:458) · [test_release.py:286](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:286) · [test_release.py:328](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:328) · [test_release.py:367](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:367) · [test_release.py:568](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:568) · [test_release.py:639](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:639) · [test_release.py:701](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:701)\n\n**The report also quotes the preceding run’s timings.** The new release/library seconds are `8.55/6.69`, `6.76/5.09`, `6.90/5.46`, and `4.48/3.51` in table order. The actual range is **1.26–1.33×**. All four still meet both budgets. The package counts, byte sizes, dated answers, closing result, and 257 label-matching fields holding 32 distinct texts checked out. The subsequent full-suite run passed 425 tests. [Report table:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:57) · [old-1:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:19) · [old-2:11071](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:11071) · [old-3:17267](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:17267) · [served:30199](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23c/results.json:30199) · [Full-suite output:2](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/buduqedk6.output:2)"}}
